/*  EXPECTED: COMPILES and runs; compiled output must match the interpreter.

    An object made in a rabbit holds a series from outside in one field and its own in the other.
    A rabbit's series goes into its own one.

    Each field of an object written out is judged by what that field was given, not by the
    longest-lived thing anywhere in the object (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O2). */

Define object pair-of-rows with (the series of series of number near, the series of series of number far).
Define outer as a series of series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define both as a new pair-of-rows { the near a series of series of number, the far outer }.
    Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
    Insert inner into both's near.
    State the number of both's near.
Done.

/*  Make and drop enough values that freed memory is handed out again. */
Define churn as a series of text.
Define tick as 0.
While tick is less than 400, repeat:
    Insert ("zzzzzzzz" joined to "yyyyyyyy") into churn.
    tick becomes tick + 1.
Done.
